  m_text: Tuberculosis can be prevented by screening regularly for those at risk
    of developing TB. If TB is contracted, maintaining good hygiene, seeking well-ventilated
    spaces, isolating at home, and wearing face masks or covering one's mouth when
    coughing and sneezing is important. Vaccinations are also a good method of prevention.
